25,2,1,talk,Kenji,,It looks like our yards are a mess of old gear and we can't afford a winter cutover. We need something rugged.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"Interesting. The board ignores operating costs but cuts capital. Also, separate licenses seem to drive prices up over time.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"As I feared, support is fragmented and our requirements shift too fast for frozen scopes. We need a single point of accountability.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Rin,,"The old dispatch tool is stuck in time, and that external data move in 2018 was a total disaster!","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Servas,,"We are losing our experts and the crews ignore trainers. We need a partner who stays on-site, not just visitors.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Asuka, if the scope changes fast, will a rigid system fail us in the yard?","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Servas, if we can't hire admins, does that mean we should avoid systems we have to host ourselves?","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Kenji, yes. A fixed configuration that doesn't evolve will be bypassed by spreadsheets again.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Mizuki, if the board likes operating costs, maybe a subscription is better than a big purchase?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Mizuki, exactly. Without internal staff, we cannot manage our own servers. We need external stability.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Kenji,,I just want to make sure the vendor understands that November to January is a no-go zone for changes.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Rin, subscriptions are easier to approve, but I'm worried about those yearly price climbs on add-ons.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,Asuka,,We need a vendor that handles the migration and the support under one roof to avoid the finger-pointing.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Rin,,"I agree! No more ""outside teams"" who leave us with broken route codes.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Servas,,A vendor with an engineering team present through the rollout would help the supervisors actually adopt the system.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
