50,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"Candidate C has an engineering team on-site, but Candidate D is a hosted suite. I'm leaning toward C for the yard support.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"Candidate A is a subscription, but B's modular licensing sounds like the price-climb trap I found in the invoices.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Candidate A has a partner for migration and training, but D's fixed configuration is exactly what I'm afraid of.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Rin,,Candidate C is built for transport! That sounds way better than a general tool that gets ignored.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Servas,,Candidate C's on-site team solves my concern about the supervisors and the retiring administrators.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Mizuki, would C's on-premise model be too expensive for the board's capital budget?","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"Possibly, but the renewal invoices showed that outright purchases only cost maintenance. It might be the cheapest long-term.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Servas, does C provide a single point of support, or is it still fragmented?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Rin,,I like C because it's specialized. A and B feel too generic.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Servas,,"C's engineering team stays through the rollout, which provides the accountability Asuka wants.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Kenji,,I'm sold on C. It's the only one that feels like it survives the depot floor.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"If it avoids the modular price hikes of B and the hidden costs of A, I'll support C.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"If the engineering team handles the ""who is in charge"" problem, C is the logical choice.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Rin,,C it is! Let's go with the transport specialists.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Servas,,"I agree. The human transition is the hardest part, and C addresses it best.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
